# .env.example -- template for the secrets BOTH stages share.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then paste your values into .env
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# One file at the repo root serves training/ and verification/ alike. Each
# stage's submit.sh and Makefile source `../.env` relative to itself, so there
# is exactly one place to paste a key and exactly one file to rotate.
#
# .env is gitignored (root .gitignore: `.env`, `.env.*`, `!.env.example`);
# this template, with no real values, is the committed one.
#
# Values are quoted on purpose: the NYU presigned URLs contain & and ?, which
# an unquoted shell assignment treats as operators. Keep the quotes.
#
# NEVER paste any of these into a .sub file. They reach a job through HTCondor
# `getenv` from your shell, so they appear in the job ClassAd (condor_q -l),
# readable by you and CHTC admins only.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS NEEDED FOR THE LOCAL SMOKE TESTS. `make local-run`
# (verification) and `make smoke` / `make job-smoke` (training) pass
# --no_wandb and use synthetic data, so they run with an empty .env or none.

# --- Weights & Biases --------------------------------------------------------
# From https://wandb.ai/authorize.
#
# Needed for : CHTC runs in both stages. training/submit.sh and
#              verification/submit.sh refuse to submit without it unless you
#              pass OFFLINE=1, which logs offline for `wandb sync` later.
# Not needed : any local target.
#
# SECURITY (CLAUDE.md / ROADMAP.md): a W&B key from a prior project is sitting
# in public git history in Research/inpainting.sub. Rotate that key before
# using any key here, and never paste one into a .sub file.
WANDB_API_KEY=''

# Optional. Your W&B username or team name. Blank = your default entity.
WANDB_ENTITY=''

# WANDB_PROJECT is deliberately NOT set here.
#
# It is the one W&B variable that differs between the stages -- training logs
# to fastmri-varnet-train and verification to fastmri-varnet-verify. Each
# .sub file sets the right value itself (`environment = "WANDB_PROJECT=..."`),
# and train_wandb.py / verify_varnet.py default to the same two names. Setting
# it here would export one project name into both stages via getenv and land
# half your runs in the wrong place. Override it per-command if you ever need
# to (`WANDB_PROJECT=scratch ./submit.sh model1`), not in this file.

# --- fastMRI knee dataset (NYU) ----------------------------------------------
# From the approval email after applying at https://fastmri.med.nyu.edu/ and
# accepting the KNEE agreement.
#
# These are presigned S3 URLs embedding AWSAccessKeyId and Signature, so they
# ARE credentials, not just links. They expire roughly 90 days after issue
# (this batch around 2026-12-08); re-request from fastmri@med.nyu.edu after
# that. Paste them exactly as they appear, query string included.
#
# Note: the released VarNet checkpoint is NOT gated. It comes from
# dl.fbaipublicfiles.com and needs no credential -- prepare_staging.sh and
# `verify_varnet.py --download_state_dict` both fetch it directly.

# Validation split, used by verification/: prepare_staging.sh downloads the
# 94 GB val tarball with these two (the .xz and its SHA256 manifest).
FASTMRI_VAL_URL=''
FASTMRI_SHA_URL=''

# Train split, used by training/: NYU ships it as five batches,
# knee_multicoil_train_batch_0..4 (~91 GB each). Paste the presigned URL for
# knee_multicoil_train_batch_0.tar.xz -- the text between the quotes on the
# line ending in `--output knee_multicoil_train_batch_0.tar.xz`. Only
# subset_train.sub uses it (training/README.md section 3b).
FASTMRI_TRAIN_URL=''

# --- CHTC --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not a secret. Your UW-Madison NetID, used to build the /staging paths.
# prepare_staging.sh defaults to $USER on the access point if blank, and shards
# the path by the netid's first letter: apryan3 gives /staging/a/apryan3/fastmri,
# which is where the dataset lives. The group directory
# /staging/groups/kamilov_group/Kamilov-SciAI-datasets is not readable by this
# account as of 2026-09-10.
#
# STAGING_DIR (not set here) overrides the whole path: point it at a local
# directory for an off-cluster run, or at the group directory if access lands.
NETID=''
